--TEST--
a time zone written as text is checked while compiling: a name that is not a time zone, an offset past 25:59:59 and a `string` variable at a `Zone` parameter are each one diagnostic (`rule:core-classes/a-time-class-builds-its-own-values`)
--FILE--
<?nvs
var $at = Core\Time\Instant::fromEpoch(0);

// A misspelled name.
var $misspelled = $at->in('Europe/Berln');
// A name with the wrong case and a space at the end.
var $spaced = $at->in('utc ');
// An offset further from UTC than any zone is.
var $far = $at->in('+26:00');
// Text in a variable is not a zone. `Core\Time\Zone::of` converts it.
var $name = 'Europe/Berlin';
var $variable = $at->in($name);

echo "unreachable\n";
--EXPECT--

--EXPECTF-ERROR--
error[E0769]: this text is not valid for this function: `Europe/Berln` is not a time zone name
%A
  = help: Time zone names close to this text: `Europe/Berlin`, %s

error[E0769]: this text is not valid for this function: `utc ` is not a time zone name
%A
  = help: Time zone names close to this text: `UTC`.

error[E0769]: this text is not valid for this function: `+26:00` is not a zone offset. An offset is written `+HH:MM` and is at most 25:59:59 from UTC
%A
error[E0401]: expected `Core\Time\Zone`, found `string`
%A
error: aborting due to 4 errors
To read what a code means and how to fix it, run `nvs agent show <code>`.
